be2-47b2-bb22-07f0df2e5b90","position":{"commit_sha":"e356e601a6581cea97ff5e73d610e328d70da39c","position":"1784609134064177001-f622a385-cbe2-47b2-bb22-07f0df2e5b90"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"91d85a6461f794883d0e4911162247bb435c00001efbb8cdb7633307bcb73c3c","event_uuid":"83c9e953-eb21-4eb7-9269-20a371896cef","position":{"commit_sha":"a0ef5ff52b16f80ae5bc58301420fc43fbd11fdf","position":"1784609134798670001-83c9e953-eb21-4eb7-9269-20a371896cef"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-216_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"42587558-4191-4a14-bbfd-728d8d0007b7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","body":"Operational provisioning COMPLETED 2026-07-10 ~17:50-18:00 UTC (AWS root session + JoeOakhartNava where needed) — verification of artifact emission in flight. Details: (1) SSM slot /rebar/prod/reviewbot-tickets-pat ALREADY held a real classic PAT (ghp_, 40 chars) — validated against GitHub: push=true on navapbc/rebar. NOTE it is a broad classic repo-scope token, not the fine-grained contents:write-only PAT the design specified — least-privilege swap recommended (only a human can mint that). (2) terraform: imported the 5 pre-existing SSM params into state (ssm.tf has ignore_changes=[value], so import is the correct reconciliation — terraform no longer plans to re-create them); applied tag updates. (3) Re-ran fetch-secrets.sh (ENV_FILE=/opt/rebar/infra/compose/.env): .env now carries REVIEWBOT_TICKETS_PAT. (4) Restarted review-bot; entrypoint materialized the persistent tickets worktree (295M clone onto the gerrit_reviewbot_tickets volume) and /review/health is 200. (5) Forced a re-review of merged change 492 via /rerun (202 accepted) to prove artifact write+push. AC2 (env delivery on deploy without manual boot — autodeploy re-runs fetch-secrets before compose up) remains the code portion of this ticket.","timestamp":1783706160793800001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","body":"END-TO-END PROOF COMPLETE (2026-07-10 21:04 UTC): forced re-review of merged change 492 emitted the first REAL production code_review artifact — ticket 8e68-601a-b32d-4302 (type code_review, title 'code-review: rebar~492 @ 40e42c962...', Decision PASS, change_fingerprint recorded), auto-linked relates_to e7f4 via the commit's rebar-ticket trailer, committed to the persistent worktree and auto-pushed to origin/tickets. Getting here required fixing a deeper defect than the missing PAT: a fresh entrypoint clone of the tickets branch is WRITE-DEAD (.env-id is gitignored -> 'ticket system not initialized'; container has no git identity -> commit fails), and emit_code_review_artifact swallows both silently — filed as bug d220-eeda-1909-4147 (discovered_from this ticket). Prod's persistent volume is now converged (ran rebar._store.ensures.run_ensures + set repo-local git identity RebarBotNava/joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com — both persist on the gerrit_reviewbot_tickets volume across restarts), but any fresh volume regresses until d220's entrypoint fix lands. AC1 is MET in prod. Remaining on this ticket: AC2 (autodeploy re-runs fetch-secrets before compose up so new env keys reach the box without a manual boot) — code work. Also recommended: swap the broad classic repo-scope PAT for a fine-grained contents:write-only token (human-mintable only).","timestamp":1783717851274835001},{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"AC2 landed and deployed. Merged to main as Gerrit change 861 (commit 820159375 'f600: autodeploy re-runs fetch-secrets before compose up'; rebar-ticket: f600 trailer; LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1; reachable from HEAD).\n\nCode (infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh): added SECRETS_PATHS trigger (fetch-secrets.sh, ssm.tf); the review-bot redeploy block now fires on 'changed BOT_PATHS || changed SECRETS_PATHS'; fetch-secrets.sh re-runs right before 'docker compose up' (after rsync, TARGET copy); on SSM failure it aborts fail-safe (err marker + record_backoff_failure, .env intact, running bot untouched, no rollback). Tests: tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_fetch_secrets.py — (a) fetch-secrets runs before compose up on a secrets-only change; (b) failure aborts without building. make lint + typecheck + the tests green.\n\nDEPLOYED to prod box i-00880b2c7f13527c5 (us-east-1) via SSM on 2026-07-21: /opt/rebar/infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh now has SECRETS_PATHS (owner 502:502, mode 755 preserved, bash -n clean, prior version backed up to .bak-f600). Triggered rebar-autodeploy.service: Result=success, ExecMainStatus=0, 'up to date; no-op', no AUTODEPLOY_ERROR, /health 200. The new fetch-secrets-before-compose-up path will fire on the next bot/secrets change.\n\nAC1 was already DONE in prod (change 492 / artifact 8e68). Out-of-scope follow-ups remain separately tracked: least-privilege PAT swap (human-only) and bug d220 (fresh-volume entrypoint write-dead).","timestamp":1784609093682325001}],"created_at":1783659016455668001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b7f184ac-ca6f-4713-bc89-10eba07c12d7","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"2731-4c53-56b4-46cc"},{"link_uuid":"86145d18-cade-4aa1-9fd8-7de0b6d54985","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"af53-cd55-48e2-4486"}],"description":"## Why\nIncident 2731's trigger commit (10837ca88) shipped the code_review artifact feature, but it was inert in prod: the box's .env had no REVIEWBOT_TICKETS_* vars. autodeploy.sh rsync-excludes infra/compose/.env (line 88) and never re-runs fetch-secrets.sh, so NO newly-added SSM-backed env key can reach the box on deploy without a manual boot — a half-updated-deploy-path defect.\n\n## Status\nAC1 (artifacts emitted from prod reviews) is DONE and proven in prod (see comments: SSM slot populated, terraform state reconciled, fetch-secrets re-run by hand, end-to-end artifact 8e68 emitted on change 492, 2026-07-10). The SSM/terraform work was OPERATIONAL and is already complete; note the slot /rebar/prod/reviewbot-tickets-pat already exists in infra/terraform/ssm.tf (rebar_secret_params, ~line 49) with lifecycle{ignore_changes=[value]}, so 'terraform apply' is a NO-OP for its value — the operative provisioning step was 'aws ssm put-parameter --overwrite --name /rebar/prod/reviewbot-tickets-pat --type SecureString --value <PAT>', NOT terraform. This is recorded for accuracy; no terraform/SSM work remains.\n\n## Remaining work (AC2 — the only code change)\nMake autodeploy re-run fetch-secrets.sh before 'docker compose up' so new/rotated SSM-backed env keys reach the review-bot container on deploy without a manual boot.\n\nPrecise design (in infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh):\n- Add a dedicated trigger SECRETS_PATHS='infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh infra/terraform/ssm.tf'. Rationale: a new env key requires editing fetch-secrets.sh (to emit the leaf) and/or ssm.tf (to declare the param); NEITHER is in BOT_PATHS, so keying the refresh only off BOT_PATHS would miss exactly the env-only-change scenario AC2 names. (Pure SSM VALUE rotation with no git change is out of scope: main does not advance, so autodeploy no-ops — that path is operator-triggered, not deploy-triggered.)\n- Guard the existing review-bot redeploy block on: changed BOT_PATHS OR changed SECRETS_PATHS (so a secrets-only change still recreates the container to pick up the new .env).\n- Placement: AFTER the rsync+chown (so $DEPLOY_REPO holds the TARGET fetch-secrets.sh) and BEFORE the ':prev' tag / 'docker compose build && up'. Invoke ENV_FILE=\"$COMPOSE_DIR/.env\" bash \"$DEPLOY_REPO/infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh\"; then re-assert the preserved .env owner.\n- Error contract (preserves autodeploy's fail-safe, never-half-updated guarantee): fetch-secrets is fail-fast — on any SSM error it exits 1 WITHOUT touching .env. On that failure, emit an err 'secrets-fetch-failed' marker, record_backoff_failure, and exit 1 — abort the deploy BEFORE tagging :prev or building, so the running bot stays on its current image (:latest untouched, nothing to roll back). Never build/up against a stale or half-written secrets file. Runs only on an actual bot/secrets redeploy (not every 2-min tick), so no SSM quota regression.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] code_review artifacts are written + pushed from prod reviews (no 'emission failed' warnings). [DONE in prod — change 492 / artifact 8e68]\n- [ ] autodeploy.sh re-runs fetch-secrets.sh before 'docker compose up' on a BOT_PATHS OR SECRETS_PATHS change; a new SSM-backed env key reaches the box on deploy without a manual boot.\n- [ ] On fetch-secrets failure the deploy aborts fail-safe (err marker + backoff, .env intact, running bot untouched, no rollback needed).\n- [ ] Tests cover: (a) fetch-secrets runs before compose up on a secrets-only change; (b) fetch-secrets failure aborts the deploy without building.\n- [ ] File paths: infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh (the code change); infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh, infra/terraform/ssm.tf (referenced/triggering, unchanged).\n\n## Out of scope / follow-ups\n- Least-privilege PAT swap (broad classic repo-scope -> fine-grained contents:write only): human-mintable only; recommended, tracked separately.\n- Bug d220 (entrypoint clone write-dead on a FRESH volume): separate ticket; prod volume already converged.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","af53-cd55-48e2-4486"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"f622a385-cbe2-47b2-bb22-07f0df2e5b90","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f600-525c-fd6d-4a3d","ticket_type":"task","title":"activate the reviewbot durable-tickets feature: SSM PAT + terraform apply + fetch-secrets rerun; fix .env delivery gap in autodeploy","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["45dac057-3898-4ced-a464-f0b1dc0be092","b7f184ac-ca6f-4713-bc89-10eba07c12d7","2dd417d8-5914-4788-8f74-f5f840088534","316a6486-d938-425d-9979-a2b588f0b250","fb52ed23-1958-4a54-8d5a-73af55a0aa09","f87630eb-e3a9-44f2-a33b-1a9f10b228c7","d10c0af8-22b0-4789-8bbb-2e6acd5a81ce","8ffab323-81b5-48eb-bb92-c693fad33a7d","bcabe8ec-bff4-4703-acff-78762cbda579","9838a0b7-a606-4362-a541-f0d19fe2b750","0923b63e-09e6-4167-8580-3f7084215633","86145d18-cade-4aa1-9fd8-7de0b6d54985","cd3c21e2-1d59-48bf-9e9b-fbeb950d109d","881eeba7-1b8d-4e84-a031-71ce2382ba69","1e85764d-6f90-4c30-88d3-cc1292aac9df","f622a385-cbe2-47b2-bb22-07f0df2e5b90","83c9e953-eb21-4eb7-9269-20a371896cef","8bd46b94-8fc2-4d16-bcc0-ff7716850d2b","2fc0f1a2-da23-40dd-9fe5-e69a39207de5","5fdd7eb0-7d90-4321-9c39-9a750d8a08ad","4eb6854e-5761-4e7c-aeca-99cdd7d7d56d","3827d295-78b9-4bab-a219-3fc2c14ed5d8","82c7ce01-13b4-4110-85e3-c020893e4347","bc013221-d2d0-4dc5-8996-97c44bd0aeaa"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785993190943099001,"uuid":"ead59fe6-3384-4deb-b1e8-051767589447"}